{"timestamp":"2026-09-17T16:30:22.662Z","ordinal":16392,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a0aa80-3aab-7313-9603-edf7533a1570","turn_id":"01a0b034-33c3-7cc0-b8f9-f6db910f9861","item":{"type":"Extension","kind":"web.search","id":"exec-f8e3b4a3-2958-4657-a3db-fe56b6cb393d","query":"https://docs.entire.io/cli/installation","action":{"type":"openPage","url":"https://docs.entire.io/cli/installation"},"results":[{"type":"text_result","domain":"docs.entire.io","ref_id":"turn51view0","snippet":"Total lines: 294","thumbnail_url":"https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-1/REDACTED","title":"Installation - Entire","url":"https://docs.entire.io/cli/installation"}]},"started_at_ms":1789662622002,"completed_at_ms":1789662622661}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-17T16:30:22.729Z","ordinal":16393,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a0b034-7409-77d3-8d8a-6c2b92519c8f","call_id":"call_ak4ZM4nX0NIkhL1Oh2CctMka","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.7 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Installation - Entire (https://docs.entire.io/cli/installation)\nciteturn51view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://docs.entire.io/cli/installation\",\"lineno\":null}); Redirected to URL: https://docs.entire.io/installation; Total lines: 294\nL0: > ## Documentation Index\nL1: >\nL2: > Fetch the complete documentation index at: cite0†/llms.txt L3: >\nL4: > Use this file to discover all available pages before exploring further.\nL5: \nL6: cite1†Skip to main content L7: \nL8: cite2†Entire home page L9: \nL10: Search...\nL11: \nL12: Navigation\nL13: \nL14: Getting Started\nL15: \nL16: Installation\nL17: \nL18: Getting Started\nL19: \nL20: # Installation\nL21: \nL22: Install, update, verify, and uninstall the Entire CLI.\nL23: \nL24: Copy page Copy page\nL25: ##\nL26: \nL27: cite3†​ L28: \nL29: System Requirements\nL30: \nL31:   * macOS, Linux, or Windows\nL32:   * Git 2.25 or later\nL33:   * Bash, Zsh, Fish, or PowerShell\nL34:   * Windows PowerShell 5.1 or later, for the Windows PowerShell installer\nL35: Building from source requires Go 1.26.6 or later.\nL36: ##\nL37: \nL38: cite4†​ L39: \nL40: Release Channels\nL41: \nL42: Entire ships two release channels:\nL43: \nL44:   * `stable`: the default channel for Homebrew, Scoop, `install.sh`, and `install.ps1`\nL45:   * `nightly`: prerelease builds available through Homebrew, `install.sh`, and `install.ps1`\nL46: Scoop supports the stable channel only. For a nightly install on Windows, use `install.ps1`.\nL47: ##\nL48: \nL49: cite5†​ L50: \nL51: Install and Update Entire\nL52: \nL53: Choose one installation method. Use the update command in the same tab when you want a newer release.\nL54: \nL55:   * macOS with Homebrew\nL56: \nL57:   * Linux Install Script\nL58: \nL59:   * Linux Direct Download\nL60: \nL61:   * Windows with PowerShell\nL62: \nL63:   * Windows with Scoop\nL64: \nL65:   * Build from Source\nL66: \nL67: Install the stable channel:\nL68: \nL69:     `brew install --cask entireio/tap/entire\nL70:     `\nL71: \nL72: Or install the nightly channel:\nL73: \nL74:     `brew install --cask entireio/tap/entire@nightly\nL75:     `\nL76: The fully qualified cask name adds the `entireio/tap` tap for you, so no separate `brew tap` step is needed.Update the channel you installed:\nL77: \nL78:     `brew upgrade --cask entireio/tap/entire\nL79:     `\nL80: \nL81:     `brew upgrade --cask entireio/tap/entire@nightly\nL82:     `\nL83: \nL84: Install the stable channel:\nL85: \nL86:     `curl -fsSL https://entire.io/install.sh | bash\nL87:     `\nL88: \nL89: Or install the nightly channel:\nL90: \nL91:     `curl -fsSL https://entire.io/install.sh | bash -s -- --channel nightly\nL92:     `\nL93: The script installs `entire` and `git-remote-entire` in `~/.local/bin`. If that directory is missing from your `PATH`, the script prints the command that adds it to your shell configuration.Run the command for your channel again to update Entire.\nL94: Download the stable AMD64 archive and install both executables:\nL95: \nL96:     `download_dir=\"$(mktemp -d)\"\nL97:     mkdir -p \"$HOME/.local/bin\"\nL98:     curl -fsSL https://github.com/entireio/cli/releases/latest/download/entire_linux_amd64.tar.gz \\\nL99:       -o \"$download_dir/entire_linux_amd64.tar.gz\"\nL100:     tar -xzf \"$download_dir/entire_linux_amd64.tar.gz\" -C \"$download_dir\"\nL101:     install -m 0755 \"$download_dir/entire\" \"$download_dir/git-remote-entire\" \"$HOME/.local/bin/\"\nL102:     rm -rf \"$download_dir\"\nL103:     `\nL104: For ARM64, replace `amd64` with `arm64` in the archive name:\nL105: \nL106:     `download_dir=\"$(mktemp -d)\"\nL107:     mkdir -p \"$HOME/.local/bin\"\nL108:     curl -fsSL https://github.com/entireio/cli/releases/latest/download/entire_linux_arm64.tar.gz \\\nL109:       -o \"$download_dir/entire_linux_arm64.tar.gz\"\nL110:     tar -xzf \"$download_dir/entire_linux_arm64.tar.gz\" -C \"$download_dir\"\nL111:     install -m 0755 \"$download_dir/entire\" \"$download_dir/git-remote-entire\" \"$HOME/.local/bin/\"\nL112:     rm -rf \"$download_dir\"\nL113:     `\nL114: Run the block for your architecture again to update Entire.\nL115: \nL116: Install the stable channel from Windows PowerShell 5.1 or later:\nL117: \nL118:     `irm https://entire.io/install.ps1 | iex\nL119:     `\nL120: \nL121: Or install the nightly channel:\nL122: \nL123:     `iex \"& {$(irm https://entire.io/install.ps1)} -Channel nightly\"\nL124:     `\nL125: For the stable channel, the script uses Scoop when Scoop is on your `PATH`, and it adds the Entire bucket first. Without Scoop, and for every nightly install, the script verifies the release checksum, installs `entire.exe` and `git-remote-entire.exe` in `%USERPROFILE%\\.local\\bin`, and adds that directory to your user `PATH`. Restart your terminal after the script changes your `PATH`.The script accepts these options.\nL126: Pass them with the script block form shown for the nightly channel, because `irm | iex` cannot forward arguments:\nL127: Option  | Effect\nL128: --- | ---\nL129: `-Channel`  | Release channel to install, `stable` or `nightly`. Defaults to `stable`.\nL130: `-InstallDir`  | Destination for a checksum verified install. Defaults to `$HOME\\.local\\bin`. Passing it selects the release archive even when Scoop is available.\nL131: `-NoPathUpdate`  | Leave your user `PATH` unchanged. Applies to release archive installs, because Scoop manages its own `PATH` entry.\nL132: `-Help`  | Print the usage message.\nL133: In Git Bash, MSYS, or Cygwin, `install.sh` stops and points you to this installer.\nL134: \nL135: Run the command for your channel again to update Entire.\nL136: \nL137: These commands drive Scoop directly. The PowerShell installer already uses Scoop for stable installs when Scoop is available.Add the Entire bucket once, then install the stable channel:\nL138: \nL139:     `scoop bucket add entire https://github.com/entireio/scoop-bucket.git\nL140:     scoop install entire/entire\nL141:     `\nL142: Update Scoop and Entire:\nL143: \nL144:     `scoop update\nL145:     scoop update entire\nL146:     `\nL147: \nL148: Use `entire/entire` for new installations. Scoop previously used `entire/cli`.\nL149: \nL150: Install both executables:\nL151: \nL152:     `go install github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire@latest\nL153:     go install github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/git-remote-entire@latest\nL154:     `\nL155: \nL156: Go writes them to `$(go env GOPATH)/bin`. Add that directory to your `PATH` if your shell cannot find `entire`.Run both commands again to update the source installation.\nL157: ##\nL158: \nL159: cite6†​ L160: \nL161: Verify the Installation\nL162: \nL163: Run:\nL164: \nL165:     `entire version\nL166:     `\nL167: \nL168: Entire CLI 0.10.5 prints three lines. The Go version and platform reflect the release and system you installed:\nL169: \nL170:     `Entire CLI 0.10.5\nL171:     Go version: go1.26.6\nL172:     OS/Arch: darwin/arm64\nL173:     `\nL174: \nL175: Release archives also include `git-remote-entire`. Git invokes this helper when a remote uses an `entire://` URL. Verify that your shell can find both executables:\nL176: \nL177:   * macOS or Linux\nL178:   * Windows\nL179: \nL180:     `command -v entire\nL181:     command -v git-remote-entire\nL182:     `\nL183: ##\nL184: \nL185: cite7†​ L186: \nL187: Installation and Data Locations\nL188: \nL189: The executable location depends on the installation method:\nL190: \nL191: Method  | Location\nL192: --- | ---\nL193: Homebrew  | The Homebrew prefix returned by `brew --prefix`\nL194: Linux install script or direct download  | `~/.local/bin`\nL195: Windows PowerShell script without Scoop  | `%USERPROFILE%\\.local\\bin`, or the `-InstallDir` you passed\nL196: Scoop  | The directory returned by `scoop prefix entire`\nL197: Go  | `$(go env GOPATH)/bin`\nL198: Entire stores repository settings in `.entire/settings.json` and personal repository overrides in `.entire/settings.local.json`. See cite8†Local, Project, and Global Settings for those files. The CLI also uses these directories for each user:\nL199: Data  | Default  | Override\nL200: --- | --- | ---\nL201: Login contexts, update state, and file based credentials  | `~/.config/entire`  | `ENTIRE_CONFIG_DIR`\nL202: Discovery caches  | `~/.cache/entire`  | `XDG_CACHE_HOME`, with `/entire` appended\nL203: Managed CLI plugins on macOS and Linux  | `~/.local/share/entire/plugins`  | `ENTIRE_PLUGIN_DIR`, or `XDG_DATA_HOME` with `/entire/plugins` appended\nL204: \nL205: `XDG_CONFIG_HOME` does not change the Entire config directory. Set `ENTIRE_CONFIG_DIR` when you need a different location.\nL206: ##\nL207: \nL208: cite9†​ L209: \nL210: Control Update Prompts\nL211: \nL212: Set this variable in scripts, CI, or other environments where the CLI should not prompt for an update:\nL213: \nL214:     `ENTIRE_NO_AUTO_UPDATE=1\nL215:     `\nL216: ##\nL217: \nL218: cite10†​ L219: \nL220: Shell Completion\nL221: \nL222: Entire generates shell completion scripts for Bash, Zsh, Fish, and PowerShell with cite11†`entire completion` . The steps below cover Bash and Zsh.\nL223: \nL224:   * Bash\nL225: \nL226:   * Zsh\nL227: \nL228: Add this command to `~/.bashrc`:\nL229: \nL230:     `source <(entire completion bash)\nL231:     `\nL232: \nL233: Add this command to `~/.zshrc`:\nL234: \nL235:     `source <(entire completion zsh)\nL236:     `\nL237: ##\nL238: \nL239: cite12†​ L240: \nL241: Uninstall Entire\nL242: \nL243: Use the command that matches your installation method.\nL244: \nL245:   * Homebrew\nL246: \nL247:   * Linux Install Script or Direct Download\nL248: \nL249:   * Windows PowerShell Script\nL250: \nL251:   * Scoop\nL252: \nL253:   * Go\nL254: \nL255: Stable:\nL256: \nL257:     `brew uninstall --cask entireio/tap/entire\nL258:     `\nL259: \nL260: Nightly:\nL261: \nL262:     `brew uninstall --cask entireio/tap/entire@nightly\nL263:     `\nL264: \nL265:     `rm -f \"$HOME/.local/bin/entire\" \"$HOME/.local/bin/git-remote-entire\"\nL266:     `\nL267: Remove both executables from the directory you installed them in:\nL268: \nL269:     `Remove-Item \"$HOME\\.local\\bin\\entire.exe\", \"$HOME\\.local\\bin\\git-remote-entire.exe\"\nL270:     `\nL271: \nL272: The user `PATH` entry for that directory remains. Remove it if you no longer need the directory. If the script used Scoop, follow the Scoop tab instead.\nL273: \nL274:     `rm -f \"$(go env GOPATH)/bin/entire\" \"$(go env GOPATH)/bin/git-remote-entire\"\nL275:     `\nL276: Uninstalling the executables does not remove repository settings, checkpoints, or user data. Inspect the paths under cite7†Installation and Data Locations before removing data you no longer need.\nL277: ##\nL278: \nL279: cite13†​ L280: \nL281: Review Recent Changes\nL282: \nL283: Read the cite14†Entire CLI changelog†github.com for changes in each release. Continue to the cite15†Quickstart to capture your first checkpoint.\nL284: \nL285: Was this page helpful?\nL286: \nL287: Yes No\nL288: \nL289: cite15†Quickstart Previous cite16†Entire CLI and entire.io Next L290: \nL291: [Input: Ask a question...]\nL292: \nL293: cite17†x†x.com cite18†github†github.com cite19†discord†discord.gg cite20†linkedin†www.linkedin.com cite21†website†entire.io "}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0b034-33c3-7cc0-b8f9-f6db910f9861","create_time":1789662622.729818}}}
