{"timestamp":"2026-09-17T16:30:29.399Z","ordinal":16399,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a0aa80-3aab-7313-9603-edf7533a1570","turn_id":"01a0b034-33c3-7cc0-b8f9-f6db910f9861","item":{"type":"Extension","kind":"web.search","id":"exec-30f0b9fd-3f09-45db-b302-823e312f1304","query":"","action":{"type":"other"},"results":[{"type":"text_result","domain":"docs.entire.io","ref_id":"turn52view0","snippet":"Total lines: 306","thumbnail_url":"https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-1/REDACTED","title":"Local, Project, and Global Settings - Entire","url":"https://docs.entire.io/guides/configuration/settings-layers"}]},"started_at_ms":1789662628446,"completed_at_ms":1789662629399}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-17T16:30:29.460Z","ordinal":16400,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a0b034-8e54-7f12-bfe0-0ae0d90fc1b7","call_id":"call_A270iWPIyJRA1FrsSdM94Qbh","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 1.0 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Local, Project, and Global Settings - Entire (https://docs.entire.io/guides/configuration/settings-layers)\nciteturn52view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn51view0\",\"id\":8}); Total lines: 306\nL0: > ## Documentation Index\nL1: >\nL2: > Fetch the complete documentation index at: cite0†/llms.txt L3: >\nL4: > Use this file to discover all available pages before exploring further.\nL5: \nL6: cite1†Skip to main content L7: \nL8: cite2†Entire home page L9: \nL10: Search...\nL11: \nL12: Navigation\nL13: \nL14: Configuration\nL15: \nL16: Local, Project, and Global Settings\nL17: \nL18: Configuration\nL19: # Local, Project, and Global Settings\nL20: \nL21: Configure shared repository behavior, personal overrides, and the files Entire writes under .entire.\nL22: \nL23: Copy page Copy page\nL24: \nL25: Entire uses a layered configuration system that allows project-wide settings to be shared via Git while supporting personal overrides. Use this page when you are deciding whether a setting should apply to everyone on the project, only to your machine, or to all repositories you work in.\nL26: \nL27:   * Local Settings\nL28: \nL29:   * Project Settings\nL30:   * Global Settings\nL31: \nL32: Local settings have the highest priority and are used for personal preferences, private rules, machine-specific paths, and temporary debugging.\nL33: ##\nL34: \nL35: cite3†​ L36: \nL37: Local Settings File\nL38: \nL39: Local settings are stored in `.entire/settings.local.json` and are automatically ignored by Git.Local settings are merged with project settings. You only need to specify the settings you want to override:\nL40: \nL41: .entire/settings.local.json\nL42: \nL43:     `{\nL44:       \"log_level\": \"debug\",\nL45:       \"telemetry\": false\nL46:     }\nL47:     `\nL48: ##\nL49: \nL50: cite4†​ L51: \nL52: Local Settings Reference\nL53: \nL54: Use these settings locally when the behavior should not affect teammates.\nL55: Setting path  | Type  | Use for  | Learn more\nL56: --- | --- | --- | ---\nL57: `commit_linking`  | string  | Personal commit-linking behavior during `git commit`  | cite5†Capture Sessions and Their Checkpoints L58: `strategy_options.push_sessions`  | boolean  | Checkpoint push behavior only on your machine  | cite6†Checkpoint Storage L59: `strategy_options.checkpoint_remote`  | object  | Personal checkpoint remote while testing storage behavior  | cite7†Checkpoint Storage L60: `redaction.pii.enabled`  | boolean  | Optional PII redaction for your own captured sessions  | cite8†Privacy and Redaction L61: `redaction.custom_redactions`  | object  | Private regex redaction rules that should not be committed  | cite9†Privacy and Redaction L62: `redaction.externalize_images`  | boolean  | Move inline base64 images into the checkpoint asset store on your machine  | cite10†Privacy and Redaction L63: `redaction.openai_privacy_filter`  | object  | Personal OpenAI Privacy Filter settings, including `prompt_default`  | cite11†Privacy and Redaction L64: `redaction.openai_privacy_filter.command`  | string  | Path to your `opf` binary. Read only from an untracked local settings file  | cite12†Privacy and Redaction L65: `telemetry`  | boolean/null  | Personal analytics preference in this repository  | cite13†Privacy and Redaction L66: `sign_checkpoint_commits`  | boolean  | Personal checkpoint commit signing preference  | cite14†Privacy and Redaction L67: `log_level`  | string  | Temporary debug logging without changing team settings  | cite15†Logging and Diagnostics L68: `external_agents`  | boolean  | Agent integration discovery only on your machine  | cite16†Set Up an Agent L69: `absolute_git_hook_path`  | boolean  | Full `entire` binary path in Git hooks for GUI Git clients on your machine  | cite17†Git Hooks L70: ##\nL71: \nL72: cite18†​ L73: \nL74: Modify Local Settings\nL75: \nL76:   * Use the CLI\nL77: \nL78:   * Edit JSON\nL79: \nL80: Add `--local` when the command should write to `.entire/settings.local.json`.\nL81: \nL82:     `entire configure --local --telemetry=false\nL83:     entire configure --local --skip-push-sessions\nL84:     entire configure --local --absolute-git-hook-path\nL85:     `\nL86: \nL87: If a setting does not have a CLI flag, edit `.entire/settings.local.json` directly.\nL88: \nL89: Edit `.entire/settings.local.json` directly:\nL90: \nL91:     `vim .entire/settings.local.json\nL92:     `\nL93: Top-level settings are written directly:\nL94: \nL95: .entire/settings.local.json\nL96: \nL97:     `{\nL98:       \"log_level\": \"debug\"\nL99:     }\nL100:     `\nL101: \nL102: Dotted setting paths are written as nested objects:\nL103: \nL104: .entire/settings.local.json\nL105: \nL106:     `{\nL107:       \"redaction\": {\nL108:         \"custom_redactions\": {\nL109:           \"private_codename\": \"PROJECT_[A-Z]{4}\"\nL110:         }\nL111:       }\nL112:     }\nL113:     `\nL114: ##\nL115: \nL116: cite19†​ L117: \nL118: Verify Local Settings\nL119: \nL120: After editing local settings, run:\nL121: \nL122:     `entire status --detailed\nL123:     `\nL124: \nL125: Use this to confirm Entire is still reading the repository configuration. If the behavior does not match `.entire/settings.local.json`, check the setting name and JSON nesting. Local settings override project and global settings for the same setting path.\nL126: Project settings apply to the current repository and are used for shared behavior such as checkpoint storage, team redaction rules, and default repository behavior.\nL127: ##\nL128: \nL129: cite20†​ L130: \nL131: Project Settings File\nL132: \nL133: Project settings are stored in `.entire/settings.json`.When Entire creates project settings, the file starts with:\nL134: \nL135: .entire/settings.json\nL136: \nL137:     `{\nL138:       \"enabled\": true\nL139:     }\nL140:     `\nL141: \nL142: Most projects can start here. Add settings only when the repository should share that behavior.\nL143: ##\nL144: \nL145: cite21†​ L146: \nL147: Project Settings Reference\nL148: \nL149: Use these settings in `.entire/settings.json` when the behavior should apply to the whole project.\nL150: Setting path  | Type  | Default  | Description  | Learn more\nL151: --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nL152: `enabled`  | boolean  | `true`  | Whether Entire is active in this repository  | cite20†Local, Project, and Global Settings L153: `commit_linking`  | string  | `\"prompt\"`  | Controls whether Entire prompts before linking a Git commit to recent agent session context  | cite5†Capture Sessions and Their Checkpoints L154: `strategy_options.push_sessions`  | boolean  | `true`  | Automatically push checkpoint data when someone runs `git push`  | cite22†Session Storage L155: `strategy_options.checkpoint_remote`  | object  | `null`  | Push checkpoint data to a separate repository  | cite7†Checkpoint Storage L156: `strategy_options.summarize.enabled`  | boolean  | `false`  | Auto-generate checkpoint summaries at commit time  | cite23†Session Storage L157: `redaction.betterleaks.enabled`  | boolean  | `true`  | Run Betterleaks for secret pattern matching  | cite24†Privacy and Redaction L158: `redaction.goredact.enabled`  | boolean  | `false`  | Run goredact for secret pattern matching  | cite24†Privacy and Redaction L159: `redaction.pii.enabled`  | boolean  | `false`  | Enable optional PII redaction on top of always-on secret redaction  | cite8†Privacy and Redaction L160: `redaction.custom_redactions`  | object  | `{}`  | Add shared regex rules that replace matches with `REDACTED`  | cite9†Privacy and Redaction L161: `redaction.externalize_images`  | boolean  | `false`  | Move inline base64 images out of transcripts into the checkpoint asset store  | cite10†Privacy and Redaction L162: `redaction.openai_privacy_filter.enabled`  | boolean  | `false`  | Run the OpenAI Privacy Filter over checkpoints at push time  | cite11†Privacy and Redaction L163: `checkpoints.primary.type`  | string  | `git-refs` on first-time setup  | Checkpoint storage backend: `git-refs` or `git-branch`  | cite25†Session Storage L164: `telemetry`  | boolean/null  | `null`  | Send anonymous usage analytics for this repository  | cite13†Privacy and Redaction L165: `sign_checkpoint_commits`  | boolean  | `true`  | Sign checkpoint commits using your existing Git signing key  | cite14†Privacy and Redaction L166: `log_level`  | string  | `\"info\"`  | Log verbosity: `debug`, `info`, `warn`, `error`  | cite15†Logging and Diagnostics L167: `external_agents`  | boolean  | `false`  | Enable discovery of `entire-agent-<name>` agent integrations from `$PATH`  | cite16†Set Up an Agent L168: `absolute_git_hook_path`  | boolean  | `false`  | Embed the full `entire` binary path in Git hooks for GUI Git clients  | cite17†Git Hooks L169: ##\nL170: \nL171: cite26†​ L172: \nL173: Modify Project Settings\nL174: \nL175: To enable agent integration discovery in project settings, add:\nL176: \nL177: .entire/settings.json\nL178: \nL179:     `{\nL180:       \"external_agents\": true\nL181:     }\nL182:     `\nL183: \nL184:   * Use the CLI\nL185: \nL186:   * Edit JSON\nL187: \nL188: Add `--project` when the command should write to `.entire/settings.json`.\nL189: \nL190:     `entire configure --project --checkpoint-remote github:owner/repo\nL191:     entire configure --project --skip-push-sessions\nL192:     entire configure --project --telemetry=false\nL193:     `\nL194: If a setting does not have a CLI flag, edit `.entire/settings.json` directly.\nL195: \nL196: Edit `.entire/settings.json` directly:\nL197: \nL198:     `vim .entire/settings.json\nL199:     `\nL200: \nL201: Top-level settings are written directly:\nL202: \nL203: .entire/settings.json\nL204: \nL205:     `{\nL206:       \"telemetry\": false\nL207:     }\nL208:     `\nL209: \nL210: Dotted setting paths are written as nested objects:\nL211: \nL212: .entire/settings.json\nL213: \nL214:     `{\nL215:       \"strategy_options\": {\nL216:         \"push_sessions\": false\nL217:       }\nL218:     }\nL219:     `\nL220: ##\nL221: \nL222: cite27†​ L223: \nL224: Verify Project Settings\nL225: \nL226: After editing project settings, run:\nL227: \nL228:     `entire status --detailed\nL229:     `\nL230: \nL231: Use this to confirm Entire is still reading the repository configuration. If the behavior does not match `.entire/settings.json`, check for an override in `.entire/settings.local.json`. Local settings have higher priority than project settings.\nL232: \nL233: Global settings apply to all repositories and are used for personal defaults that should apply across projects.\nL234: ##\nL235: \nL236: cite28†​ L237: \nL238: Global Settings File\nL239: \nL240: Global settings are stored in `~/.config/entire/settings.json`.Use global settings for personal defaults that should apply across repositories.Example:\nL241: \nL242: ~/.config/entire/settings.json\nL243: \nL244:     `{\nL245:       \"telemetry\": false\nL246:     }\nL247:     `\nL248: ##\nL249: \nL250: cite29†​ L251: \nL252: Global Settings Reference\nL253: \nL254: Use global settings for personal defaults that should apply unless a project or local setting overrides them.\nL255: \nL256: Setting path  | Type  | Default  | Description\nL257: --- | --- | --- | ---\nL258: `telemetry`  | boolean  | `false`  | Default telemetry setting for new repositories\nL259: ##\nL260: \nL261: cite30†​ L262: \nL263: Modify Global Settings\nL264: \nL265:   * Use the CLI\nL266: \nL267:   * Edit JSON\nL268: \nL269: `entire configure` updates repository settings. There is no global flag for `entire configure`, so edit `~/.config/entire/settings.json` directly.\nL270: \nL271: Create the config directory if it does not exist, then edit the file:\nL272: \nL273:     `mkdir -p ~/.config/entire\nL274:     vim ~/.config/entire/settings.json\nL275:     `\nL276: \nL277: Example:\nL278: \nL279: ~/.config/entire/settings.json\nL280: \nL281:     `{\nL282:       \"telemetry\": false\nL283:     }\nL284:     `\nL285: ##\nL286: \nL287: cite31†​ L288: \nL289: Verify Global Settings\nL290: \nL291: After editing global settings, run this from an Entire-enabled repository:\nL292: \nL293:     `entire status --detailed\nL294:     `\nL295: \nL296: Use this to confirm Entire is still reading configuration. Global settings apply only when the same setting is not set in `.entire/settings.json` or `.entire/settings.local.json`.\nL297: \nL298: Was this page helpful?\nL299: \nL300: Yes No\nL301: \nL302: cite32†Configuration Previous cite33†Entire-Generated Files Next L303: \nL304: [Input: Ask a question...]\nL305: cite34†x†x.com cite35†github†github.com cite36†discord†discord.gg cite37†linkedin†www.linkedin.com cite38†website†entire.io "}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0b034-33c3-7cc0-b8f9-f6db910f9861","create_time":1789662629.460163}}}
