{"timestamp":"2026-09-17T16:30:32.554Z","ordinal":16406,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a0aa80-3aab-7313-9603-edf7533a1570","turn_id":"01a0b034-33c3-7cc0-b8f9-f6db910f9861","item":{"type":"Extension","kind":"web.search","id":"exec-08189714-5fc4-47bf-8d16-1e1e07f6acf8","query":"","action":{"type":"other"},"results":[{"type":"text_result","domain":"docs.entire.io","ref_id":"turn53view0","snippet":"Total lines: 58","thumbnail_url":"https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-1/REDACTED","title":"Entire-Generated Files - Entire","url":"https://docs.entire.io/guides/configuration/entire-files"}]},"started_at_ms":1789662631852,"completed_at_ms":1789662632554}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-17T16:30:32.623Z","ordinal":16407,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a0b034-9aaf-7eb3-b786-2c156b26b26b","call_id":"call_CESIxuZ0wOe9462p97ocVZ3J","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.8 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Entire-Generated Files - Entire (https://docs.entire.io/guides/configuration/entire-files)\nciteturn53view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn52view0\",\"id\":33}); Total lines: 58\nL0: > ## Documentation Index\nL1: >\nL2: > Fetch the complete documentation index at: cite0†/llms.txt L3: >\nL4: > Use this file to discover all available pages before exploring further.\nL5: \nL6: cite1†Skip to main content L7: \nL8: cite2†Entire home page L9: \nL10: Search...\nL11: \nL12: Navigation\nL13: \nL14: Configuration\nL15: \nL16: Entire-Generated Files\nL17: \nL18: Configuration\nL19: # Entire-Generated Files\nL20: \nL21: Decide which Entire-generated files belong in Git and which should stay on your machine.\nL22: \nL23: Copy page Copy page\nL24: \nL25: Entire creates a small set of repository files for configuration, redaction rules, diagnostics, and local runtime state. Commit files that define shared project behavior. Keep personal overrides, logs, temporary files, and machine-local state out of Git.\nL26: ##\nL27: \nL28: cite3†​ L29: \nL30: Commit or Keep Local\nL31: Path  | Commit?  | Use for\nL32: --- | --- | ---\nL33: `.entire/settings.json`  | Yes, when Entire is part of the project  | Shared project settings, such as checkpoint storage, team redaction rules, and default repository behavior\nL34: `.entire/.gitignore`  | Yes  | Keeping local Entire files out of normal commits\nL35: `.entire/redactors/`  | Yes, for shared rule packs  | Team redaction rules that should apply to everyone working in the repository\nL36: `.entire/settings.local.json`  | No  | Personal overrides, debug logging, private rules, and machine-specific settings\nL37: `.entire/redactors/local/`  | No  | Personal redaction rule packs\nL38: `.entire/logs/`  | No  | Local diagnostic logs\nL39: `.entire/tmp/`  | No  | Temporary runtime files\nL40: `.entire/metadata/`  | No  | Local metadata generated while Entire runs\nL41: `.entire/current_session`  | No  | Pointer to your current local session\nL42: If you are trying Entire locally before adopting it for the project, keep `.entire/settings.json` local until the team decides to share Entire configuration.\nL43: ##\nL44: \nL45: cite4†​ L46: \nL47: Files Stored Elsewhere\nL48: Checkpoint data is not committed from your working tree. Entire stores checkpoint metadata in Git refs under `refs/entire/checkpoints/`, or on the `entire/checkpoints/v1` branch for repositories on the branch backend, in your code repository or in a configured checkpoint remote. See cite5†Where your data lives . Global settings live at `~/.config/entire/settings.json`. Agent hook files live in agent-specific folders, such as `.claude/`, `.codex/`, `.cursor/`, and `.gemini/`.\nL49: \nL50: Was this page helpful?\nL51: \nL52: Yes No\nL53: cite6†Local, Project, and Global Settings Previous cite7†Git Hooks Next L54: \nL55: [Input: Ask a question...]\nL56: \nL57: cite8†x†x.com cite9†github†github.com cite10†discord†discord.gg cite11†linkedin†www.linkedin.com cite12†website†entire.io "}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0b034-33c3-7cc0-b8f9-f6db910f9861","create_time":1789662632.623743}}}
