{"timestamp":"2026-09-17T16:46:19.099Z","ordinal":16519,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a0aa80-3aab-7313-9603-edf7533a1570","turn_id":"01a0b041-4be2-75a3-add6-65c0f7a0e0f3","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0b3476aa27839743016aac195813f487d083dd659311676cbb","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"Entire itself is current: `0.10.7-nightly.202609170627.0dda4e14f`.\n\nI then ran `entire enable --force` twice. Its diagnostic also removed one genuinely stale rule from `.claude/settings.json`: `Read(./.entire/metadata/**)`, which Entire says is retired and unnecessarily caused approvals.\n\nThe remaining “Claude Code hooks out of date” warning is reproducible immediately after Entire writes the hooks. That is an Entire CLI drift/detection bug, not an outdated local install or a hook file I can safely hand-edit.\n\n`.claude/settings.json` is currently modified but uncommitted solely for that retired-rule removal and key reordering. I left it uncommitted rather than silently treating generated Claude configuration as repository-owned."}],"phase":"final_answer"},"started_at_ms":1789663576148,"completed_at_ms":1789663579099}}
