{"timestamp":"2026-09-17T16:56:43.658Z","ordinal":16561,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a0aa80-3aab-7313-9603-edf7533a1570","turn_id":"01a0b04c-4256-76d0-9985-a44bbf8963d1","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0b3476aa27839743016aac1bca5c3087d0bb74cf59af70036f","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"I’ll apply the safe, repository-owned policy now: stop automatic checkpoint pushes to the public origin, document Entire as an optional maintainer workflow, and ignore the generated adapter outputs. I will not create a private checkpoint repository or alter the already-tracked Claude project settings without a separate explicit decision."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1789664202562,"completed_at_ms":1789664203658}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-17T16:56:43.660Z","ordinal":16562,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_0b3476aa27839743016aac1bca5c3087d0bb74cf59af70036f","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"I’ll apply the safe, repository-owned policy now: stop automatic checkpoint pushes to the public origin, document Entire as an optional maintainer workflow, and ignore the generated adapter outputs. I will not create a private checkpoint repository or alter the already-tracked Claude project settings without a separate explicit decision."}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0b04c-4256-76d0-9985-a44bbf8963d1","create_time":1789664183.756226,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-17T16:56:46.066Z","ordinal":16563,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0b3476aa27839743016aac1bcba48087d0865b4f0de821cb3d","status":"completed","call_id":"call_i93jHhEvy6YvaCewQEkQ8ktw","name":"exec","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({\"cmd\":\"rtk fd -a 'CONTRIBUTING.md|DEVELOPMENT.md|justfile' . && rtk sed -n '1,180p' .entire/settings.json && rtk sed -n '1,180p' CONTRIBUTING.md 2>/dev/null || true && rtk sed -n '1,180p' .gitignore && rtk git diff -- .claude/settings.json\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":40000});\ntext(r.output);","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0b04c-4256-76d0-9985-a44bbf8963d1","create_time":1789664183.756226}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-17T16:56:46.154Z","ordinal":16564,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a0aa80-3aab-7313-9603-edf7533a1570","turn_id":"01a0b04c-4256-76d0-9985-a44bbf8963d1","session_id":"01a0aa80-3aab-7313-9603-edf7533a1570","root_turn_id":"01a0b04c-4256-76d0-9985-a44bbf8963d1","response_id":"resp_0b3476aa27839743016aac1bb76f6087d09c549947c0d6c74c","usage":{"input_tokens":184996,"cached_input_tokens":184064,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1185,"reasoning_output_tokens":979,"total_tokens":186181},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":184996,"cached_input_tokens":184064,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1185,"reasoning_output_tokens":979,"total_tokens":186181},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":253367297,"cached_input_tokens":249359488,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":554204,"reasoning_output_tokens":189974,"total_tokens":253921501}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-17T16:56:46.259Z","ordinal":16565,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a0aa80-3aab-7313-9603-edf7533a1570","turn_id":"01a0b04c-4256-76d0-9985-a44bbf8963d1","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-f5df2f5a-297e-45a5-8cc0-c2c38019e8fc","process_id":"37677","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","rtk fd -a 'CONTRIBUTING.md|DEVELOPMENT.md|justfile' . && rtk sed -n '1,180p' .entire/settings.json && rtk sed -n '1,180p' CONTRIBUTING.md 2>/dev/null || true && rtk sed -n '1,180p' .gitignore && rtk git diff -- .claude/settings.json"],"cwd":"file:///Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"rtk fd -a 'CONTRIBUTING.md|DEVELOPMENT.md|justfile' . && rtk sed -n '1,180p' .entire/settings.json && rtk sed -n '1,180p' CONTRIBUTING.md 2>/dev/null || true && rtk sed -n '1,180p' .gitignore && rtk git diff -- .claude/settings.json"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/CONTRIBUTING.md\n/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/justfile\n{\n  \"enabled\": true,\n  \"telemetry\": false,\n  \"checkpoints\": {\n    \"primary\": {\n      \"type\": \"git-refs\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n<p align=\"center\">\n  <img src=\"assets/callisto-logo.png\" width=\"140\" alt=\"Callisto Release Engine Logo\" />\n</p>\n\n<h1 align=\"center\">Contributing to Callisto</h1>\n\n<p align=\"center\">\n  <b>Guidelines, engineering standards, testing expectations, and contribution workflows.</b>\n</p>\n\nBy participating in this project, you agree to abide by the [Code of Conduct](./CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md). Found a security issue? See [SECURITY.md](./SECURITY.md) instead of opening a public issue.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Development Setup & Prerequisites\n\n### Prerequisites\n\n- **Rust Toolchain**: `stable` channel (managed via `rustup`).\n- **WebAssembly Target**: `wasm32-wasip1` (for `callisto-moon` PDK plugin verification).\n- **Moon / Proto** (Recommended): Primary monorepo task runner.\n- **Just** (Recommended): Command runner for quick workspace recipes.\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> Install native local Git hooks with `just hooks` to run formatting checks automatically before every local commit (`pre-commit`) and push (`pre-push`).\n\n### Local Initial Build\n\n```bash\n# Clone the repository\ngit clone https://github.com/orin-dx/callisto.git\ncd callisto\n\n# Add WASM cross-compilation target & install local Git hooks\nrustup target add wasm32-wasip1\njust hooks\n\n# Run full local CI pipeline via Just & Moon\njust ci\n```\n\n---\n\n## 2. Primary Development Tasks (`just`)\n\nCallisto uses `just` as its canonical developer command runner, delegating workspace tasks to `moon` under the hood:\n\n| Action | Canonical Command | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Run Full Verification CI** | `just ci` | Runs formatting, Clippy lints, unit/integration tests, audit, and WASM target checks |\n| **Run Test Suite** | `just test` | Runs unit, integration, doctests, and E2E lifecycle test suites |\n| **Check Clippy Lints** | `just lint` | Runs Clippy lints with `-D warnings` across all workspace crates |\n| **Check Code Formatting** | `just fmt-check` | Verifies code formatting compliance |\n| **Format Code** | `just fmt` | Applies `cargo fmt` formatting automatically |\n| **Check Security Advisories** | `just audit` | Runs `cargo deny check advisories` security check |\n| **Verify WASM Target** | `just wasm-check` | Verifies `wasm32-wasip1` cross-compilation target |\n\n---\n\n## 3. Core Code Standards & Invariants\n\nAll contributions to Callisto must adhere to 5 strict engineering invariants:\n\n### 1. Safe Rust Only (`unsafe_code = \"forbid\"`)\nCallisto forbids `unsafe` code blocks across all 10 workspace crates. Memory safety and thread safety are guaranteed by the Rust compiler.\n\n### 2. Format Preservation Guarantee\nCallisto never uses regular expressions or line-based string manipulation to edit manifests (`Cargo.toml`, `package.json`).\n- **TOML**: Edits must use `toml_edit` to parse and manipulate Concrete Syntax Trees (CST), preserving comments, table ordering, and whitespace.\n- **JSON**: Edits must fingerprint indentation style (`IndentStyle::Tabs` vs `IndentStyle::Spaces(N)`) and preserve key insertion order using `serde_json`.\n\n### 3. Crash-Safe Atomic Disk Writes\nAll manifest and configuration modifications must go through `callisto_manifests::atomic::atomic_write`. File writes create a `NamedTempFile` in the target file's parent directory, flush data to disk, and atomically replace the target file via `fs::rename`.\n\n### 4. Direct & Actionable Diagnostics (`miette`)\nErrors intended for CLI users must derive `miette::Diagnostic` with an explicit error code, clear diagnostic message, and actionable remediation tip.\n\n### 5. Dual Licensing Tier Respect\n- **Layer 1 Crates** (`callisto-model`, `callisto-format`): Dual-licensed under `MIT OR Apache-2.0`. Must NOT depend on AGPL-licensed crates (`callisto-graph`, `callisto-cli`, `callisto-manifests`).\n- **Layer 2-4 Crates** (`callisto-graph`, `callisto-cli`, `callisto-moon`): Licensed under `AGPL-3.0-only`.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Interactive Changesets & CI Coverage\n\n### Interactive Changeset Wizard\n\nWhen adding a feature, fix, or breaking change, run `callisto add` in an interactive terminal to launch the 5-step wizard:\n\n```bash\ncargo run --bin callisto -- add\n```\n\nThis interactive wizard:\n1. Prompts for workspace package selection (MultiSelect).\n2. Asks which selected packages require a **MAJOR** bump.\n3. Asks which remaining packages require a **MINOR** bump (defaulting others to **PATCH**).\n4. Prompts for the changeset summary text.\n5. Displays a colored preview and requests confirmation before writing `.changeset/<human-slug>.md`.\n\nFor automated agent or script execution, pass explicit CLI flags:\n\n```bash\ncargo run --bin callisto -- add --package callisto-cli:minor --summary \"Add interactive wizard\"\n```\n\n### GitHub CI & Coverage Reports\n\nGitHub Actions executes CI using `just` and `moon` (`moonrepo/setup-toolchain-action` and `extraactions/setup-just`), ensuring total parity between local developer environments and CI.\n\nIn addition, every pull request generates:\n- **Test Summary Cards**: Published directly to GitHub Step Summaries.\n- **Code Coverage Reports**: Generated via `taiki-e/cargo-llvm-cov-action@v1` and attached as `lcov.info` build artifacts.\n/target\n/bin\n.DS_Store\n\n# moon\n.moon/cache\n.moon/docker\n\n# generated artifacts\n*.wasm\ncallisto-schema.json\nlcov.info\n\n# unfixed-bug ledger — deliberately kept out of this public repo, lives at\n# /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto-findings/FINDINGS.md\n.agents/skills/bug-hunter/FINDINGS.md\n\n# per-session parallel-agent worktree checkouts — full repo copies, never committed\n.claude/worktrees/\n.playwright-mcp/\nmutants.out/\n.claude/settings.json | 49 +++++++++++++++++++++++--------------------------\n 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+), 26 deletions(-)\n\nChanges:\n\n.claude/settings.json\n@@ -1,21 +1,13 @@\n {\n-  \"permissions\": {\n-    \"allow\": [\n-      \"Bash(cargo test *)\",\n-      \"Bash(just ci)\",\n-      \"Bash(cargo build *)\",\n-      \"Bash(cargo clippy *)\",\n-      \"Bash(just test)\",\n-      \"Bash(cargo nextest *)\",\n-      \"Bash(just lint)\",\n-      \"Bash(cargo check *)\",\n-      \"Bash(just fmt-check)\",\n-      \"Bash(just audit)\",\n-      \"Bash(just doc-check)\"\n-    ],\n-    \"deny\": [\n-      \"Read(./.entire/metadata/**)\"\n-    ]\n+  \"enabledPlugins\": {\n+    \"vector@orin-dx-agent-plugins\": true,\n+    \"axiom@orin-dx-agent-plugins\": true,\n+    \"canon@orin-dx-agent-plugins\": true,\n+    \"delta@orin-dx-agent-plugins\": true,\n+    \"graph@orin-dx-agent-plugins\": true,\n+    \"lambda@orin-dx-agent-plugins\": true,\n+    \"proof@orin-dx-agent-plugins\": true,\n+    \"trace@orin-dx-agent-plugins\": true\n   },\n   \"hooks\": {\n     \"PostToolUse\": [\n@@ -94,14 +86,19 @@\n       }\n     ]\n   },\n-  \"enabledPlugins\": {\n-    \"vector@orin-dx-agent-plugins\": true,\n-    \"axiom@orin-dx-agent-plugins\": true,\n-    \"canon@orin-dx-agent-plugins\": true,\n-    \"delta@orin-dx-agent-plugins\": true,\n-    \"graph@orin-dx-agent-plugins\": true,\n-    \"lambda@orin-dx-agent-plugins\": true,\n-    \"proof@orin-dx-agent-plugins\": true,\n-    \"trace@orin-dx-agent-plugins\": true\n+  \"permissions\": {\n+    \"allow\": [\n+      \"Bash(cargo test *)\",\n+      \"Bash(just ci)\",\n+      \"Bash(cargo build *)\",\n+      \"Bash(cargo clippy *)\",\n+      \"Bash(just test)\",\n+      \"Bash(cargo nextest *)\",\n+      \"Bash(just lint)\",\n+      \"Bash(cargo check *)\",\n+      \"Bash(just fmt-check)\",\n+      \"Bash(just audit)\",\n+      \"Bash(just doc-check)\"\n+    ]\n   }\n }\n  +23 -26\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/CONTRIBUTING.md\n/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/justfile\n{\n  \"enabled\": true,\n  \"telemetry\": false,\n  \"checkpoints\": {\n    \"primary\": {\n      \"type\": \"git-refs\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n<p align=\"center\">\n  <img src=\"assets/callisto-logo.png\" width=\"140\" alt=\"Callisto Release Engine Logo\" />\n</p>\n\n<h1 align=\"center\">Contributing to Callisto</h1>\n\n<p align=\"center\">\n  <b>Guidelines, engineering standards, testing expectations, and contribution workflows.</b>\n</p>\n\nBy participating in this project, you agree to abide by the [Code of Conduct](./CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md). Found a security issue? See [SECURITY.md](./SECURITY.md) instead of opening a public issue.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Development Setup & Prerequisites\n\n### Prerequisites\n\n- **Rust Toolchain**: `stable` channel (managed via `rustup`).\n- **WebAssembly Target**: `wasm32-wasip1` (for `callisto-moon` PDK plugin verification).\n- **Moon / Proto** (Recommended): Primary monorepo task runner.\n- **Just** (Recommended): Command runner for quick workspace recipes.\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> Install native local Git hooks with `just hooks` to run formatting checks automatically before every local commit (`pre-commit`) and push (`pre-push`).\n\n### Local Initial Build\n\n```bash\n# Clone the repository\ngit clone https://github.com/orin-dx/callisto.git\ncd callisto\n\n# Add WASM cross-compilation target & install local Git hooks\nrustup target add wasm32-wasip1\njust hooks\n\n# Run full local CI pipeline via Just & Moon\njust ci\n```\n\n---\n\n## 2. Primary Development Tasks (`just`)\n\nCallisto uses `just` as its canonical developer command runner, delegating workspace tasks to `moon` under the hood:\n\n| Action | Canonical Command | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Run Full Verification CI** | `just ci` | Runs formatting, Clippy lints, unit/integration tests, audit, and WASM target checks |\n| **Run Test Suite** | `just test` | Runs unit, integration, doctests, and E2E lifecycle test suites |\n| **Check Clippy Lints** | `just lint` | Runs Clippy lints with `-D warnings` across all workspace crates |\n| **Check Code Formatting** | `just fmt-check` | Verifies code formatting compliance |\n| **Format Code** | `just fmt` | Applies `cargo fmt` formatting automatically |\n| **Check Security Advisories** | `just audit` | Runs `cargo deny check advisories` security check |\n| **Verify WASM Target** | `just wasm-check` | Verifies `wasm32-wasip1` cross-compilation target |\n\n---\n\n## 3. Core Code Standards & Invariants\n\nAll contributions to Callisto must adhere to 5 strict engineering invariants:\n\n### 1. Safe Rust Only (`unsafe_code = \"forbid\"`)\nCallisto forbids `unsafe` code blocks across all 10 workspace crates. Memory safety and thread safety are guaranteed by the Rust compiler.\n\n### 2. Format Preservation Guarantee\nCallisto never uses regular expressions or line-based string manipulation to edit manifests (`Cargo.toml`, `package.json`).\n- **TOML**: Edits must use `toml_edit` to parse and manipulate Concrete Syntax Trees (CST), preserving comments, table ordering, and whitespace.\n- **JSON**: Edits must