{"timestamp":"2026-09-17T16:57:44.470Z","ordinal":16600,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a0aa80-3aab-7313-9603-edf7533a1570","turn_id":"01a0b04c-4256-76d0-9985-a44bbf8963d1","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0b3476aa27839743016aac1c053d2887d09f37ff844854dc82","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"Implemented and committed: `711d2f5 docs(entire): keep session data off public origin`.\n\n- Automatic Entire checkpoint pushing is disabled.\n- The 17 existing checkpoints will remain local and will not sync to public `origin`.\n- Generated local agent adapters are ignored.\n- `CONTRIBUTING.md` documents Entire as optional and requires an approved private checkpoint remote before synchronization.\n\nThis follows Entire’s shared-config/local-state guidance. [Entire generated files](https://docs.entire.io/guides/configuration/entire-files) [Entire settings](https://docs.entire.io/guides/configuration/settings-layers)\n\nOne unrelated generated diff remains in `.claude/settings.json`: the Entire diagnostic removed its retired metadata deny rule, but Entire still falsely reports hook drift after regeneration. I left that uncommitted rather than hand-editing generated hook configuration."}],"phase":"final_answer"},"started_at_ms":1789664261299,"completed_at_ms":1789664264470}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-17T16:57:44.474Z","ordinal":16601,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_0b3476aa27839743016aac1c053d2887d09f37ff844854dc82","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"Implemented and committed: `711d2f5 docs(entire): keep session data off public origin`.\n\n- Automatic Entire checkpoint pushing is disabled.\n- The 17 existing checkpoints will remain local and will not sync to public `origin`.\n- Generated local agent adapters are ignored.\n- `CONTRIBUTING.md` documents Entire as optional and requires an approved private checkpoint remote before synchronization.\n\nThis follows Entire’s shared-config/local-state guidance. [Entire generated files](https://docs.entire.io/guides/configuration/entire-files) [Entire settings](https://docs.entire.io/guides/configuration/settings-layers)\n\nOne unrelated generated diff remains in `.claude/settings.json`: the Entire diagnostic removed its retired metadata deny rule, but Entire still falsely reports hook drift after regeneration. I left that uncommitted rather than hand-editing generated hook configuration."}],"phase":"final_answer","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0b04c-4256-76d0-9985-a44bbf8963d1","create_time":1789664256.717656,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}}}
